  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given, $\\rho, q$ are roots of equation $x^{2}+p x+q=0$\r\n$\\therefore \\quad p+q=-p \\Rightarrow 2 p+q=0$\r\n$\\begin{array}{lr}\\text { and } & p q=q \\\\ \\Rightarrow & \\rho=1\\end{array}$\r\nPut $p=1$ in Eq, we get $2 \\times 1+q=0$\r\n$\\begin{array}{lr}\\Rightarrow & q+2=0 \\\\ \\Rightarrow & q=-2 \\\\ \\text { Hence, } p=1, q=-2\\end{array}$",
    "image": null
  },
